# How you can contribute

AACSearch is everything that it is because of the support of our community. Whether we look at our Discord community, GitHub contributors, or developers interacting with us on social media, everyone adds value and makes a difference. If you would like to increase your participation and play a more substantial role in the development of AACSearch, here are some ways you can make a difference:

- Share your suggestions in the [issues](https://github.com/aacsearch/aacsearch/issues) listed on our GitHub repo.
- Make bug fixes and feature contributions by creating [pull requests](https://github.com/aacsearch/aacsearch/pulls).
- Raise feedback and new ideas about AACSearch in our [GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/aacsearch/aacsearch/discussions).
- Participate with other AACSearch developers in our [Discord community](https://aacsearch.io/discord).
- Share your AACSearch project with our community on the [Built With AACSearch](https://builtwith.aacsearch.io/) platform.
- Add any AACSearch-related educational content on our [awesome-aacsearch](https://github.com/aacsearch/awesome-aacsearch) repo.

Together, let’s continue to build AACSearch through the power of open source, allowing every developer to have the capabilities of hundreds of developers through one platform.
